[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to camera, introducing the video's premise.
AUDIO: 'X Tool sent me this wild machine that claims it can print my art on pretty much anything. Clothes, jackets, hats, and maybe some things that absolutely shouldn\'t have art on it. But before I become a fullblown one-man apparel company, let\'s find out what this thing can actually handle. I grabbed a bunch'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of random thrift store clothes, some weird stuff from around my studio, more than a little bit of my own clothes. I grabbed a few things that may be dangerous to transfer onto, but I\'m doing it for you and cuz it\'ll be fun. So, this could go great or it could'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'explode spectacularly. I guess we just have to find out. I\'ve been interested in DTF printers for a while now. Being able to make custom one-off things or [music] just fully create my own merch by myself has always sounded very'

